# Copy to .env on the edge VPS and fill in real values before running:
#   docker compose up -d --build
#
# This is the EDGE VPS's env file -- separate from the root .env.example,
# which is the APP VPS's. See deploy/edge/README.md for why the split
# exists and how the two hosts talk to each other.

# --- Domains (Caddy issues real TLS certs for these via Let's Encrypt --
# they must already point at THIS (edge) VPS's IP before you start the
# stack, not the app VPS's). Must be byte-for-byte identical to the
# APP_DOMAIN/API_DOMAIN values in the app VPS's own .env -- the backend uses
# APP_DOMAIN for CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS/FRONTEND_URL, and the frontend uses it
# at runtime to tell its own platform domain apart from a tenant's custom
# domain (see frontend/src/proxy.ts).
APP_DOMAIN=app.example.com
API_DOMAIN=api.example.com
ACME_EMAIL=ops@example.com

# --- App VPS address ---
# Where this Caddy forwards traffic to. Prefer the app VPS's PRIVATE network
# IP if your hosting provider offers one between VPS's on the same account
# (DigitalOcean, Hetzner, Vultr, Linode all do, usually free) -- otherwise
# its public IP, in which case you MUST firewall ports 3000/8000 on the app
# VPS to only accept connections from this edge VPS's IP (see
# deploy/edge/README.md). Never leave those ports open to the whole
# internet: that bypasses TLS entirely and serves the app in plaintext.
APP_UPSTREAM_HOST=10.0.0.2
